From: Aamir <aamir@tallow-lang.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:58:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/27] docs: P2.T3/T4 verified, including the defect the
 refusal test found

T3 passes 2/0 with the three graded assertions (both legs exit 0 with no fallback, stdout
byte-identical, and a pinned reference matched over four discriminating documents).

T4 passes only because the test found a real defect: extract(42) exited 0 and printed
false in the interpreter, refused in the compiled path, and passed tallow check. The
interpreter arm was coercing the argument and fabricating a plausible value. The plan
records all three behaviours before and after, plus the two limits that bound what the
test can promise: the type checker does not enforce the declared type, and argument
coercion is the interpreter's convention at 549 sites, so the sibling question is a
language-level audit rather than part of this binding.
